let's take a break from the monsterverse  and go into another monster universe in  this video today i will be talking about  one of hp lovecraft's most intriguing  and mysterious characters aside  azeroth is just one of many diverse and  interesting characters within the  cthulhu mythos  that we will be exploring in this and  other upcoming videos  the cthulhu universe is a vast one with  many strange  or inspiring and terrifying deities and  creatures  here i will be talking about the origins  nature and powers of this particular  character  and what sets him apart from other  characters in this universe  the name azdoth is first mentioned by  h.b lovecraft himself  in a note in 1919 where he describes the  name as being hideous  but the first actual appearance of  azdoth as a proper character in  lovecraft's fiction  is in the story the dream quest of  unknown kadat  here the author describes this deity as  a sultan ruler of a realm beyond the one  we models are familiar with lovecraft  explains that this  realm is one marked by chaos and  confusion the opposite of our own  it is from this story that one of  azeroth's many names  the demon sultan is also derived  azeroth is known as the nuclear chaos  the blind idiot god  but just to be clear lovecraft was not  thinking of atomic power when he was  describing azeroth  in the story of the whisperer in  darkness the word nuclear can be seen as  a reference to the center of the cosmos  in which this god resides now the  reference to azdoth as being  blind and an idiot can be seen in the  story the haunt of the dark  and as darth is also described as being  mindless in the dream of the witch house  the name the blind idiot god however  must not be equated with the idea that  azeroth must be somehow stupid  we must keep in mind that lovecraft was  an atheist and hence for him  the universe is not characterized by  some kind of ultimate meaning  as a dot then can be seen as a living  force whose ultimate book has a living  force whose ultimate purpose  our destiny is not clear or even evident  at all  this is what partly contributes to the  mystery and confusion surrounding his  character  gods are usually portrayed as having a  goal or a tendency towards one  however in azeroth's case there is no  conscious driving towards one  he just simply exists now all gods have  their own age distinctive abilities and  powers  accordingly the deities in this  mythological universe are divided into  four  major groups the outer gods the elder  gods  the great old ones and the other gods  are the great ones  the outer gods are those who have been  in existence far  longer than the actual beginning of this  universe itself  one can even go so far as to say that  they are primeval in nature  keep in mind that while the terms the  outer gods and the other gods are used  interchangeably at times by some people  the former are more powerful than the  latter  at times one gets the impression that  aztar thoughts and even cthulhu himself  since he has been described as being  cosmically boundless and there is an  inclination to think of him as being  omnipotent as well  this is especially true if we take into  consideration that asda's real name  is rather a mystery and that it is not  listed even in a necronomicon  however it is believed that his real  name if it is ever to be mentioned will  instill fear in the hearts of both  men and gods hence one can view aside as  being a formidable opponent for  anything for the other gods the great  old ones  since he might be the father of all  creation and we live in his dream  one of the factors we must take into  account is that other writers have also  contributed to this universe  among them is august derelict who wrote  the novel the lurker in the threshold  here as doth is depicted as in a similar  fashion  to john milton's lucifer in paradise  laws both  take on the role of a rebel and are  punished for it while lucifer is sent to  hell as punishment by the christian god  jin god azeroth is made blind and  mindless by the elder gods  if we consider derelict's addition to  the mythology then omnipotence is not  the word  which we can use to describe as doth  this however does not make him any less  close to omnipotence it is also reminded  that the powers of such mythological  characters  are subject to change depending on who  writes them as  readers our perception of their strength  and gifts will also change accordingly  when it comes to azeroth there is no  real standard  with which to compare his powers it is  not simply a matter of measuring  physical strength and speed  but one can argue that such a  character's abilities would partly  depend on the reader's imagination as  well  as dot is in some way a puzzle  that the reader must seek to solve on  his or her own  lastly there is the popular view that  aston actually created the universe and  all its contents to his dreams  as long as he sleeps and is kept at  peace by the music of his servants the  music of his servants the world will  continue as it is  his waking up is akin to an apocalypse  where the entire world  and the universe will cease to exist  this is a point that is very similar to  the philosopher  berkeley's idea that perception is  existence  it also reminds us of the simulation  theory where the universe is just  a simulation of some unknown technician  of some higher beings  extra-dimensional beings and it is a  very terrifying thought indeed  so azeroth is one of lovecraft's most  endearing creations  he is haunting while his true form  remains somewhat in the shadows and its  nightmarish  there is also more to be said about this  deity and others in the mythos  they are all connected as darth nair  lethal cthulhu  nigrath and others so now we have come  to the end of this video  do hit that like button for support  subscribe to be a part of this mind cue  family  and hit that bell button for regular  updates on monster videos  right 